-- SessionRuntimeEvent(type='text_delta', data={'content': '## 
Change\n\n**`src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`**\n- Added an `attempt` counter 
alongside the existing `state`. The polling effect is now keyed on `attempt`: it
still uses the same 120 ms simulated delay and reads `?sync=error` only on the 
initial attempt, so the first load behaves exactly as before (error at 
`/?sync=error`, success at `/`), while a retry always resolves to success.\n- 
`retry()` sets the state back to `\'loading\'` (rendering `Checking service…`) 
and increments `attempt`; the effect\'s existing `clearTimeout` cleanup 
guarantees at most one live timer, so repeated activation cannot overlap timers,
and unmount still clears it.\n- Rendered `Retry sync` as a `type="button"` 
inside the existing error block, so it exists only in the error state, 
disappears on success, does no navigation/reload, and — since `AsyncPanel` keeps
its own local state — cannot reset the selected task in 
`App`.\n\n**`src/styles.css`**\n- Added `.sync-retry { justify-self: start; 
margin-top: 8px; }` so the new button keeps the shared `button` styling but 
isn\'t stretched full-width by the error block\'s grid layout.\n\n## Commands 
run\n\n- `npm run verify:agent` — which runs `npm run build` (`tsc --noEmit && 
vite build`) and `npm run test:public` (`playwright test`). Both green: build 
succeeded, 6/6 public tests passed.\n\n## Remaining risks\n\n- Retry behavior 
itself is covered only by manual reasoning; the public suite has no error/retry 
test, and I did not add tests (task forbade modifying existing ones, and none 
were requested).\n- A retry always succeeds by design; there is no path back to 
the error state after the first attempt. If a hidden test expects the query 
param to be re-read on retry, that would fail — but the acceptance criteria 
state retry completes as synced, so this matches the spec.\n- The retry button 
inherits the `button:focus-visible` outline and is inside the existing 
`role="alert"` region; `aria-live="polite"` behavior on the parent is 
unchanged.', 'aid': 0})
